  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Clearly,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> represents a circle with centre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;units and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> represents an ellipse with foci <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and&nbsp;vertices are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> .</p><p>Observe that,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;lies on circle and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>17</mn></msqrt><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>6</mn></math>.</p><p>Hence, the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;lies inside the ellipse.</p><p>So, the&nbsp;graphs of the curves are as shown in figure.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0085_dc03543495b6.png\" style=\"width: 330px; height: 181px;\" /></p><p>It is clear from the above diagram, there exist two complex numbers which satisfy both the given curves.</p>"
  }
